// Currently you cannot use undefined at the syntactic top level,
// because it has polymorphic type.
//
// Which is to say it fails anyway, because for some reason the check
// involved happens at runtime rather than in the typechecker.
//
// See #2425.
//
// As of 20261030 after changing how undefined is implemented, this
// now trips on undefined first before it hits the polymorphism
// check. But that could change again in the future...

undefined;
